Subject: [PATCH 2/6] Value numbering: the available-expression walk alone
 (#2924)

The owner kept value numbering's scalar walk as its one implementation
(#2924, 7112387760): over Tier 1's pipeline on sqlite3.c, Lua and musl,
it took 0.87 to 0.93 times the congruence solver's ticks in every size
bin, with every object byte-identical (6987893038). #3433 is the
vectorized form that would have to win, and recover the solver's phi
congruences.

The solver goes: #866's acyclic numbering, the refinement rounds, their
eight-lane key hashing, bounded grouping and sorted completion, and
IrGvnOptions' scalar, complete, sweep_limit and probes with the result's
counters. The walk keeps the sixteen-lane classification and the
`vectors` filter's kernel, and its keys lose the parent-class word that
only the rounds set.

Under `pressure`, a refused value now keeps the class of the expression
it matched, as the solver's "computed as without it" did: test-ir-optimize's
gvn-pressure pair, frozen from the solver, needs it (two sums of a value
and equal constants merge). The walk passes the optimizer's internals
their scalar twins, as it did when measured, until #2924's next piece.

test-ir-gvn checks each fixture once, against the interpreter and the
digest the previous commit froze. Callers drop the flag: Tier 1's three
calls (c_check_tier1.c), the tests, ir_metamorphic.c,
benchmark-ir-optimize-passes, and benchmark-ir-source, whose gvn variant
has no twin now; test-ir-source --passes checks that the result promotes.

