+## Available expressions
+
+The pass walks the dominator tree from the entry, a block at a time, with the
+expressions available there in a hash table. An instruction's key is its
+opcode, type, flags and alignment, its static payload (a constant's value, a
+parameter's or symbol's index, a comparison's predicate, an intrinsic's kind,
+an address's offset and scale), and its operands' classes; an impure
+instruction's key also holds its own number, so it matches nothing. A value's
+class is its own number, or that of the dominating equal expression it joins:
+an instruction whose key equals an available one becomes that one's alias.
+Hashes select a bucket only; full keys, and all 64 bytes of a vector constant,
+are compared on every collision. The entries a block inserted leave the table
+when its dominator subtree is done, so equal expressions in sibling blocks
+stay separate. A phi is its own value, and so is every value in a block no
+walk reaches.
+
+Until #2924 this walk was the scalar twin of a congruence solver: the coarsest
+partition stable under operand classes (#866's acyclic numbering, then
+refinement rounds for the values that reach a cycle), which also merged equal
+phis and equivalent cyclic recurrences. On Tier 1's pipeline over `sqlite3.c`,
+Lua and musl (#2924's [6987893038](https://github.com/buster14a/buster/issues/2924#issuecomment-6987893038)),
+the walk took 0.87 to 0.93 times the solver's ticks in every size bin, and every
+object was byte-identical either way, so the owner kept the walk alone. A
+vectorized value numbering that wins at every size, and recovers the phi
+congruences, is #3433. The measurements below that compare the two are the
+solver's record.
 
